    "result_text": "Done. Build is green.\n\n## What I changed\n\nOne file, one method: `AdjustOwnerRegistrationDate.service`.\n\nThe method previously handled only weekends with fixed offsets (Sat +2, Sun +1). I replaced that with a loop that rolls the date forward one day at a time while it lands on a Saturday, Sunday, or a listed public holiday \u2014 matching the reference `toBusinessDay` helper the tests use. I added the fixed holiday set (`2026-01-01, 2026-01-26, 2026-04-25, 2026-12-25, 2026-12-28`) as a private constant on the class.\n\nThe loop is essential (not just an added `contains` check): a holiday can roll onto a weekend, or a weekend onto a holiday, so it must keep advancing until it reaches a genuine business day.\n\n## Structural impact\n\n- **1 file touched.**\n- **1 function changed**, and it's the only method in its class, so `WMC_other` is 0 \u2192 `max(WMC_other, 1) = 1`. No surrounding class complexity to pay for.\n- The holiday list lives in a `static final` constant, adding no branching to the method itself.\n\nFull suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, including the `coreDefaultDateIsBusinessDay` invariant test).",
